## Current lab-observed work

| Area | Classification | Position on 2026-07-17 |
|---|---|---|
| **Huey Brain** | Current lab reality | Lenovo Legion Go running Debian; active V1 orchestration node |
| **V1 input** | Current active proof | Known MP3 fixture |
| **Transcription** | Current active proof | Local transcription; fidelity matters, not only process completion |
| **Response** | Current active proof | API-backed response path with provider selection kept replaceable |
| **Evidence** | Current active proof | Structured run log with attributable stages and failure information |
| **Huey Body** | Current physical reality | Real robotic shell, formerly Huey Core; paused for V1 |
| **LabTech** | Current support reality | External tooling including iMac 5K 2017 and Briefcase |

## Active direction

| Area | Classification | Position |
|---|---|---|
| **Huey node** | Accepted-direction candidate | One coherent embodied AI unit is the primary architectural unit |
| **Huey V4** | Active physical direction | Physical-cohesion program; not complete and not required for the current V1 proof |
| **PyHuey** | Primary GUI direction | Intended operator surface and core-runtime component; integration remains evidence-gated |
| **HueyNexusController** | Maintained project target | Nexus 5 and Nexus 7 family; OS, battery, security, and protocol validation incomplete |
| **HIMS** | Active architecture / incomplete runtime | Messaging foundations exist; authenticated controller transaction path is not complete |
| **Huey Farm** | Optional target infrastructure | Not required for node validity and not an operational collective substrate |

## Deferred unless deliberately reactivated

- live microphone input;
- wake-word processing;
- PyGPT-net as the primary interface;
- a general HIMS runtime rollout beyond bounded work;
- Huey Body actuation;
- multi-agent governance.

## Unresolved

- the final V1 declaration threshold;
- exact V4 hardware integration;
- accelerator acquisition and workload partitioning;
- controller kernel, image, provisioning, and recovery paths;
- HIMS authentication and authorization design;
- canonical memory placement and retention;
- namespace synchronization from `huey` toward `hueyos`.
